      "answer": "Reflection tokens in SELF-RAG are special tokens inserted into the original corpus by a trained critic model, used to guide the language model to retrieve, generate, and critique text passages and its own generation during training and inference [1]. They enable self-reflection by allowing the model to assess its own predictions after each generated segment [1]. These tokens are used to decide when to retrieve, evaluate relevance, support, and usefulness of generated text, and customize model behavior at test time [3][5].",
